#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""raincheck: the next hours of rain in your terminal, from Buienradar.

  raincheck               the rain at home, live: the radar map plays the
                          next two hours above the chart of the next three;
                          the first time, raincheck asks where home is
  raincheck gent          somewhere else
  raincheck sint niklaas  a place name may be several words
  raincheck 51.05,3.72    coordinates
  raincheck work          a place you saved under a name of your own
  raincheck --home gent   save Gent as home and show it right away
  raincheck --save work brussel
                          save Brussel as work, from then on: raincheck work
  raincheck --search bergen
                          list every Bergen and pick one, also with --home
                          or --save to save the one you pick
  raincheck --places      list your saved places, with --short only names
  raincheck --forget work forget a saved place
  raincheck --trip 25     when to leave to stay dry on a 25-minute trip;
                          with --short it exits with 2 when you cannot leave
                          right now
  raincheck --once        the map and the chart once, then back to the prompt
  raincheck --live        the live screen, which plain raincheck opens in a
                          terminal
  raincheck --short       only the summary, for a status bar or prompt
  raincheck --json        the forecast as JSON, for scripts
  raincheck --color       colour even when the output is not a terminal,
                          such as in watch -c raincheck --color; --no-color
                          for none at all
  raincheck --completions zsh
                          tab completion for zsh, bash or fish, see the README
  raincheck --version     the version of raincheck

In the live screen the left and right arrows or the scroll wheel move
through the hours and pause the map there, space plays it again, up and
down go through your saved places, / searches a place, s saves it, r
fetches again and q quits. + and - zoom the map in and out around the
place on screen, h, j, k and l or a drag with the mouse move it, and c
brings it back to the place.
Piped into another command, raincheck prints the chart as text.

Saved places, home among them, are kept in ~/.config/raincheck/places.json.
A forecast is reused for five minutes from ~/.cache/raincheck, and shown from
there when Buienradar cannot be reached.
Works in the Netherlands, Belgium and the border regions, as far as
Buienradar's radar reaches. Colour is dropped with NO_COLOR or when the
output is not a terminal, and kept with FORCE_COLOR.
"""
